    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Malaysia's aerospace cluster — anchored around Subang, with growing drone and UAV makers in Cyberjaya and Penang — has a quiet packaging problem. Aerospace components are simultaneously fragile, vibration-sensitive, and weight-sensitive. Foam packaging gets the cushioning right but adds weight, generates static, and creates an end-of-life waste stream that nobody wants to deal with. Honeycomb cardboard solves all three problems at once: it absorbs vibration, it's a fraction of foam's weight, and it recycles into a normal kraft stream. Quinocycle supplies aerospace MRO operations and drone OEMs across Peninsular Malaysia with custom honeycomb packaging from our Balakong factory.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Drone & UAV Airframe Protection</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Consumer-Grade Folding Drones</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Folding consumer drones (Mavic class) ship inside fitted-foam cases for retail, but B2B shipments to dealers and rental fleets need bulk-friendly outers. Honeycomb dividers between drones in a 6-unit master carton prevent rotor and gimbal damage during courier handling.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Commercial Inspection & Survey Drones</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Industrial inspection drones used by oil & gas and plantation companies in Malaysia have extended booms, RTK antennas, and gimbal payloads — all vibration-sensitive. Custom-cut honeycomb cradles built to match the airframe profile keep everything in place across rough last-mile delivery to a Sabah palm estate or Terengganu offshore base.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Agriculture Spray Drones</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Heavy spray drones (20kg+ class) shipping out to padi farms in Kedah and Perlis benefit from full honeycomb cradles with reinforced pallet bases. The combination of weight and fragile electronics makes proper bracing essential.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Aerospace MRO & Component Shipping</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Avionics & Black-Box Components</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Repaired avionics units returning to airlines from Subang MRO facilities ship in honeycomb-padded outer cartons that meet airline FAA/EASA-equivalent ASEAN standards. Honeycomb's vibration absorption protects calibration during the journey back to base.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Engine Component & Turbine Blade Outers</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Individual turbine blades, fuel pumps, and landing-gear components ship inside custom-cradled honeycomb outers. The cradle isolates the part from outer-carton wall contact, preventing surface damage that would require expensive re-inspection at receiving.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Cabin Interior & Composite Panel Shipping</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Cabin interior panels, overhead bin liners, and composite skins are large but light — perfect for honeycomb sandwich packaging. A honeycomb top sheet, a honeycomb bottom sheet, and corrugated outer give surface protection without adding meaningful weight to air freight.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Lithium Battery & Electronics Considerations</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Drones contain LiPo batteries that fall under DG (dangerous goods) air-freight rules. Honeycomb cardboard is suitable inner cushioning, but the outer packaging and labelling must meet your carrier's UN spec. We supply the honeycomb inserts; coordinate with your DG-trained shipper on the outer compliance. Many OEMs ship batteries separately to avoid the DG surcharge entirely.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="bg-surface-variant/50 border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-8 my-12">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Aerospace & Drone Spec Quick-Reference</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="font-label text-primary font-bold text-sm mb-2">CONSUMER FOLDING DRONE</p>
